    "created_at": "2020-03-19T21:14:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-19T21:14:10Z",
    "body": "I think this is actually not about \"case\" in the sense of uppercase or lowercase. This is about \"case\" as in \"which case are we in\".\r\n\r\nIn particular this is trying to specify that if you do `<el crossorigin=\"asdf\">` then `el.crossorigin === \"anonymous\"`, not `el.crossorigin === \"\"`. Both the empty string and `\"anonymous\"` are keywords mapping to the Anonymous state, but the \"canonical case\" is `\"anonyomous\"`.\r\n\r\nSo, I think it should be \"canonical keyword\". I'll post something to help.",
